# Deliberately NARROW. This repo has run without a .gitattributes under
# core.autocrlf=true for its whole life, so a broad `* text=auto` rule here would
# renormalize every tracked file at once -- a whole-tree diff that hides real changes and
# that nobody asked for. Only the paths that actually need a pin are listed.
#
# WHY tasks/ AND scripts/task.py NEED ONE (added 2026-08-23 with the task-tool trial):
# task.py's canonical frontmatter writer emits '\n' unconditionally (io.open(..., newline=''))
# and its contract is that round-tripping an untouched task file is BYTE-IDENTICAL --
# tested. Under autocrlf the working copy would hold '\r\n', so the first write op on a
# fresh clone would rewrite every line of the file it touched, turning a one-field edit
# into a whole-file diff and destroying the review property the byte-identity test exists
# to give. Pin the bytes instead of teaching the writer about platforms.
tasks/**            text eol=lf
scripts/task.py     text eol=lf
